+## 2. Full-Spectrum Evaluations
+
+### R23 · A2A v1.0.0 — exit-quarantine RFC for the R15 lane — `adapt_cleanroom` (RFC-only)
+
+**Lineage (honest chain):** R15 (#1649) evaluated A2A at the 0.3.0-era foundation stage and
+quarantined it with an explicit exit gate: *no satellite implements A2A before an RFC decision; no
+Agent Card exposure before that decision*. R23 adds the evidence R15 lacked — the spec is now
+**stable v1.0.0** (released, versioned, hosted) — and files exactly that RFC: **issue #1703**
+(parent Anchor Hub #753, synergy WO #1523).
+
+**Evidence trail (all probed 2026-10-28):**
+
+| Probe | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `GET https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/` | **200** (spec hosted, versioned pages) |
+| Spec text (raw spec doc) | "Latest Released Version **1.0.0**" with 0.3.0/0.2.6/0.1.0 predecessors |
+| `GET https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A` | **200** |
+| `rg "A2A" scripts/agents/a2a_messaging_bus.py` | internal bus exists: `.agents/a2a_inbox/{lane}.jsonl`, idempotent `message_id`, MCP-tower integration — **no Agent Card, no task lifecycle, no JSON-RPC transport** (convergent dialect, not conformance) |
+
+- **Pros:** the federation already runs an A2A-shaped internal bus, so the RFC's smallest slice
+  (one static Agent Card + one adapter module over the existing inbox contract) is native, bounded,
+  and zero-new-infra; v1.0.0 stability retires R15's "spec churn" risk; an Agent Card is the
+  natural marketplace listing artifact for WO #1523.
+- **Cons:** Agent Card exposure creates a public capability surface the Admin plane must own;
+  the internal bus's JSONL semantics (wakeup-on-tick) map awkwardly onto A2A task states — the
+  adapter must be honest about streaming/push-notification deferral.
+- **Risks:** implementation-before-decision (the exact thing R15 forbade); "A2A replaces MCP"
+  maximalism; treating the RFC as a green light for satellite-side endpoints.
+- **Anti-patterns flagged:** auto-registering agents anywhere; public endpoints that bypass the
+  tower policy plane; signed-card work before Web Bot Auth (R20/#1675) lands.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** R15's never-dos stand verbatim until #1703 is ACCEPTED: no satellite
+  implements A2A, no Agent Card is exposed, no gRPC transport work starts. This cycle files the
+  decision artifact only.
+
+**Adoption path → Issue [#1703](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1703).**
+Amends: #1649 (R15) — quarantine → RFC-on-the-table, gated on maintainer acceptance.
+
+### R24 · Aggregator tier: OpenRouter meta-lane + live direct lanes — `adapt_cleanroom`
+
+**Evidence trail (all probed 2026-10-28, unauthenticated):**
+
+| Provider | Probe | Result | Reading |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| OpenRouter | `GET /api/v1/models` | **200, 464 models** | public catalog; live ids include `glm*`, `mistralai/*`, `qwen*` — the exact families R21 hand-wired (#1685) |
+| DeepInfra | `GET /v1/openai/models` | **200, 174 models** | second public catalog, OpenAI-compatible |
+| Together | `POST /v1/chat/completions` | **401** | routable, auth-gated → valid direct lane |
+| xAI | `POST /v1/chat/completions` | **401** | routable, auth-gated → valid direct lane |
+| Groq | `POST /v1/chat/completions` | **403** | edge/WAF block, not a protocol response → **quarantine**, re-probe later |
+| Fireworks | `POST /inference/v1/chat/completions` | **404** | path dead/changed → **quarantine**, do not file |
+
+- **Pros:** one template block in `gateway/services/dynamic_ai/provider_registry.py` (the
+  registry's own doctrine — env keys, fail-closed availability — is already generic) converts
+  N integrations into 1; the 464-model unauth catalog is also the cheapest reconciliation
+  source for `model_horizon.json` drift (R21 live-flagged the mistral mismatch).
+- **Cons:** aggregator dependency (rate limits, margin pricing); catalog breadth ≠ account
+  entitlement — fail-open tiering must not assume every catalog id is routable for the tenant.
+- **Risks:** key concentration in one vendor; catalog churn inflating horizon noise; per-call
+  cost opacity vs direct lanes.
+- **Anti-patterns flagged:** treating the public catalog as entitlement truth; wiring
+  quarantined providers (groq/fireworks) without fresh probes; abandoning direct lanes for
+  strategic providers already validated (#1685).
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no auto-purchase/routing fallback that spends on the aggregator without
+  the existing budget-guard doctrine; no catalog ingestion that writes unvalidated model ids
+  into routing truth.
+
+**Adoption path → Issue [#1705](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1705).**
+Complements: #1685 (R21) — additive lanes, no overlap by construction.
